(*!
<summary>
Beckhoff EL5152: 2-channel incremental encoder interface terminal (24 V HTL, single-ended).
</summary>
<description>
Represents the 32-bit main PDOs: channel 1 uses 0x1A00/0x1600; channel 2 uses 0x1A04/0x1602.
Both channels expose counter feedback and preset without a latch. Select Standard 32-bit (MDP 511);
optional period/frequency PDOs included by the ESI preset are outside this model and must be linked
separately if retained. The Standard 16-bit image is unsupported. Link each field individually.
Evaluate bus/channel validity before use. Use one owner task and synchronize other access.
When used for I/O, link located fields or their containing buffers to the matching selected PDOs.
The record is not a packed wire buffer; compiler padding is not part of the device specification.
Unlinked/default values do not prove valid I/O. The caller evaluates bus/channel validity before use.
Use one owner task per instance and externally synchronize other access; multi-field snapshots are not atomic.
Copies store data without creating hardware links. Keep borrowed field references valid while consumers are bound.
This passive record performs no validation, synchronization, configuration or protocol advancement.
</description>
*)
TYPE EL5152 :
STRUCT
	Ch1 : INCREMENTAL_ENCODER_COUNTER_CHANNEL;
	Ch2 : INCREMENTAL_ENCODER_COUNTER_CHANNEL;
END_STRUCT
END_TYPE]]></Declaration>
  </DUT>
</TcPlcObject>
